540965 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540965 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186540552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540965 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "366ce63e-4758-55ab-ade5-2bbdeee37bb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186540551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540998 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "85c51992-c8f6-553a-ab49-de91cc2fad16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186540581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541031 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cee86ad7-df28-501c-a81c-6bd872b01f2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186540627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541039 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dcb531dc-a984-5ad5-8e3d-3ead33a40597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541093 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541093 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75253" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541093 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541093 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [0,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=20-2x-3y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541093 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "68f740c4-3eaf-53af-86af-a7b05d82500b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541093 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/29/293e79685a3f4da205d986bcf4331e4b4f43c0a48fe183d27f93aaee6bb17b99.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=4$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=4{m}_{11}+4{m}_{21}+4{m}_{12}+4{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=20-2x-3y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=20-2x-3y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/cc/cc6e04660f00d04307715159c25aa2860ca08af74ed36fc9b0be15d10ee94a27.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/74/744aeb24bb4fd4487b35ffd789d957879cb0c3ee92e40519f71b65ee5ee76dcf.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,2)=10 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(4,2)=6 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,4)=4 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(4,4)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=4\\cdot 10+4\\cdot 6+4\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0=80.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541099 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541099 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75039" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541099 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541099 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{2,3,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541099 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "73bd1c38-9ed6-5451-94fd-2aa984462a1e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541099 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/a3/a30d43569026cdf8f4ce960016620a725248726523abd005dbad5bc903123b9f.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/a8/a81396ee6d33b1ac10a44b6b8db2ded2612e86274e017ebe95c55420b7f73265.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/c9/c90a6e6d4c9e9a92bfd1c42b8350941b7d45f96d422e2a1988a4c003df6457e1.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,2)=8 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(3,2)=13 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,3)=13 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(3,3)=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =8+13+13+18 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541110 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541110 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122966" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541110 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541110 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541110 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ad4ccbd-e338-5550-8a1d-a1b82832243e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541110 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/3b/3be0ba3fa44ba61e0b55500e588387cd087b8d2f2687c5636c9b053f1f8dc5d6.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/9f/9fa44875a37e8c7b7bc69b175ac1f30fe73af936565e68ecaa82e02b7617b330.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/59/595d13ca8ec18056038a855e96ca4a3d8cc967182dae5c54b9746c731238413b.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,1)=6 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(3,1)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,2)=5 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(3,2)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=6+1+5+0=12.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541133 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541133 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122886" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541133 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541133 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c9/c9544b511212f20620d516a6f14fcfa1d812a0119cc14f8741d113c6cb663961.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541133 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cde06bdc-b497-5379-91e5-90582a7fb14e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541133 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+1\\cdot {m}_{21}+2\\cdot {m}_{12}+2\\cdot {m}_{22} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}+2{m}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541135 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541135 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122885" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541135 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541135 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b0/b00e13fc7b827b9c3960073679ee651f6bce5a6193e0b0af1907738691a287ed.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541135 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cfbdcb48-ce24-5aa4-b673-ed006db801e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541135 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=1,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=3,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+3\\cdot {m}_{21}+2\\cdot {m}_{12} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+3{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541153 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541153 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122874" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541153 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541153 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/03/03935d4a02a1a42a106e148fa120132a246818684f88a441f63de46bc01dcbdc.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541153 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f89ca459-c179-53fe-83c0-45ad6670695a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541153 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+1\\cdot {m}_{21}+1\\cdot {m}_{12}+1\\cdot {m}_{22} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186552529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186552538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186552563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186552572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186552617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1045 "Approximating Volumes Using Lower Riemann Sums" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186552529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551658 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ae59c15e-8f64-5d6d-946d-9c2353f25611" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551751 #edb/ref 1080 "32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551751 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551751 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "258f88c7-c0a2-56e8-9230-059a60c0a8e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551985 #edb/ref 1080 "24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551985 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551985 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "858f5818-4647-5518-b75d-f2e9dd90e7f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552034 #edb/ref 1080 "40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552034 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552034 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "98578764-7601-57dc-9d67-e947a3ce724a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552094 #edb/ref 1080 "36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552094 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552094 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b17bf7f2-0d3c-57ff-a579-7f0faaabe3b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552218 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552218 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552218 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ec56fda9-5a7a-576c-a3c2-f64506f5aa01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186551751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552387 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e7df747d-5ae6-580b-89b5-66c235ad174c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552488 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552488 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552488 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552488 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [1,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=9-x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,3,5\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552488 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a55a479e-4a45-5971-8018-f156cd1ee741" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552488 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/97/97220aa0d23d01e807608e6194a37661ba77cc391d0adf537908c1f13b1b6de8.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=4$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=4{m}_{11}+4{m}_{21}+4{m}_{12}+4{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=9-x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=9-x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/30/306666a0e69fca9dc47c2295aa616a944482f00b28fdd96d9d96af816b058447.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/15/15512c5f5063309474534a54b323d87c28cf9b776c10789a8f70e12cdb898aeb.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,3)=4 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(4,3)=2 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,5)=2 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(4,5)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=4\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 0=32.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552529 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186552572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552529 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "02ba616f-857b-5b1b-a652-302fd8658f7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552529 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186345055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552538 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186552563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552538 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "14825d79-a165-5a8f-bd7f-a28da631103e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552538 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186256756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552563 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6946aa2b-6720-5a06-abdf-e444f41a9ede" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552563 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186256764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552572 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186552617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552572 #edb/ref 1062 #uu